<title>NORWAY: Aker RGI sells Jotul stake at profit.</title>
<headline>Aker RGI sells Jotul stake at profit.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian holding company Aker RGI ASA said on Tuesday it had sold a 43 percent stake in stoves and fireplace manufacturer Jotul ASA.</p>
<p>The 1,251,300 shares were sold at 110 crowns per share for a total sum of 137 million crowns to a Norwegian investor.</p>
<p>Aker RGI said it would book a profit of around 90 million crowns.</p>
<p>The company said the sale was in line with its strategy to reduce the range of its interests and focus on core activities.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
